																		The SCP Christmas Art Exchange 2: Mannheim Steamrolled
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/djoric" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(388108); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=388108&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608349794" alt="Djoric" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=388108)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/djoric" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(388108); return false;" >Djoric</a></span> <span class="odate time_1385754580 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">29 Nov 2013 19:49</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1904607">
									

<p><a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fEHzYjuf5NA">You hear that?</a> It's the sound of 80s synthesized Christmas music, which means it's time once again to partake in EXTREME AMOUNTS OF JOY AND GOODWILL.</p>
<p><strong>So What Is This Thing, Anyway?</strong></p>
<p>It's a secret-santa-type gift exchange. We exchange gifts with each other, and the givers' identities remain secret until the end. (Spoil the fun and I will <em>joyfully eat your babies</em>.)</p>
<p><strong>What kinds of gifts will be exchanged?</strong></p>
<p>The exchange is for pretty much anything you can give over the internet: drawings, stories, songs, videos, whatever you feel like doing. The only requirement is that you have to make it yourself.</p>
<p><strong>How do I participate?</strong></p>
<p>Just post in this thread saying that you are interested. Your post should also include 1) What you are capable of giving (Example: I will draw or write stories / sing / interpretive dance / compose and perform epic poetry in Old English) 2) A general idea of what you want to receive. (Example: Something involving one of my SCPs / Something involving such-and-such GOI / SQUEEDLES AND MEWTS FIGHTING CRIME). This is all so I can match people up better. I can't guarantee that the matches will be perfect (you might get a story instead of a picture), but I will do my best.</p>
<p><strong>How are these distributed?</strong></p>
<p>Upon signing up, you and your preferences will be added to the MASTER EXCEL DOCUMENT OF CHRISTMAS JOY. From this, I will determine pairs for gifting, and will then send the names back to you. Once you are done with your gift, upload it to somewhere and send me a PM with a link to your gift. I will then send those out to the recipients.</p>
<p><strong>After opening</strong></p>
<p>Once you get your gift, post it in the thread, so we can all see it and have some fun trying to guess who made it and the givers can make the big reveal.</p>
<p><strong>Tentative dates:</strong></p>
<p>Final Day for Entry: December 7th<br />
Names Will Be Given Out On: December 9th<br />
Due Date: December 23rd<br />
Dispersal of Gifts: December 24th.</p>

